hadiths[45]{hadithnumber,text}:
"168","[AI-translation] The hadith of ‘Āishah, who said: When one of us was menstruating and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wished to have intimacy with her, he would command her to wrap a waist-cloth around herself during the peak of her menstruation, and then he would engage in intimacy with her. She said: ""And which of you can control his desire as the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to control his desire?"""""
"169","Ibn 'Umar announced Adhan for prayer on a cold, windy night. Then added:Pray in your dwellings; and then said: When it was a cold, rainy night, the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to command the Mu'adhdhin to say Pray in your dwellings"""""""""""""
"170","While I was lying with the Prophet (ﷺ) under a woolen sheet, I got my menses. I slipped away and put on the clothes for menses. The Prophet (ﷺ) said, Have you got your menses?"""" I replied"""""
"171","Narrated Zainab bint Abi Salama:\n\nUm-Salama said, \I got my menses while I was lying with the Prophet (ﷺ) under a woolen sheet. So I \nslipped away"""""
"172","Abu Dharr reported:The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to me: O Abu Dharr, you would soon find after me rulers who would make their prayers dead. You should say prayer at its prescribed time. If you say prayer at its prescribed time that would be a supererogatory prayer for you, otherwise you saved your prayer"""""
"173","Abu Burda b. Abu Musa al-Ash'ari reported:'Abdullah b. Umar said to me: Did you hear anything from your father narrating something from the messenger of Allah (ﷺ) about the time on Friday? I said: Yes, I heard him say from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) (these words): It is between the time when the Imam sits down and the end of the prayer"""""""""""""
"174","Narrated Ibn Abu Laila:\n\nOnly Um Hani told us that she had seen the Prophet (p.b.u.h) offering the Duha (forenoon prayer). \nShe said, \On the day of the conquest of Mecca"""""
"175","Narrated `Ali:\n\nI used to get emotional urethral discharges frequently and felt shy to ask Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) about it. So I \nrequested Al-Miqdad bin Al-Aswad to ask (the Prophet (ﷺ) ) about it. Al-Miqdad asked him and he \nreplied, \One has to perform ablution (after it).\"""""""""""""""""
"176","Abu Burda b. Abu Musa al-Ash'ari reported:'Abdullah b. Umar said to me: Did you hear anything from your father narrating something from the messenger of Allah (ﷺ) about the time on Friday? I said: Yes, I heard him say from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) (these words): It is between the time when the Imam sits down and the end of the prayer"""""""""""""
"177","Narrated `Umar bin Al-Khattab:\n\nI asked Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) \Can any one of us sleep while he is Junub?\"""" He replied """"178"""",Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) was informed that I have said: By Allah """"179"""",Narrated Anas bin Malik:\n\nThe Prophet (ﷺ) used to visit all his wives in one night and he had nine wives at that time."""""
"178","[AI-translation] The hadith of ‘Abdullāh ibn ‘Umar, who said: ‘Umar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb mentioned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he was in a state of janābah during the night, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: ""Perform ablution, wash your private part, and then sleep."""""
"179","[AI-translation] The hadith of Anas ibn Mālik, that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to visit his wives in a single night, and he had nine wives at that time."""
"180","Um-Sulaim came to Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) and said, Verily"""""
"181","Whenever the Prophet (ﷺ) finished his meals (or when his dining sheet was taken away), he used to say. Praise be to Allah Who has satisfied our needs and quenched our thirst. Your favor cannot by compensated or denied."""" Once he said"""""
"182","The hadith of Maimunah: She said: I poured water for the Prophet (peace be upon him) to perform ghusl. He poured with his right hand onto his left, and washed them both. Then he washed his private parts. Then he struck the ground with his hand, wiped it with soil, then washed it. Then he rinsed his mouth and sniffed water into his nose. Then he washed his face and poured water over his head. Then he moved aside and washed his feet. Then he was brought a towel, but he did not dry himself with it."""""
"183","Abu Burda b. Abu Musa al-Ash'ari reported:'Abdullah b. Umar said to me: Did you hear anything from your father narrating something from the messenger of Allah (ﷺ) about the time on Friday? I said: Yes, I heard him say from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) (these words): It is between the time when the Imam sits down and the end of the prayer"""""""""""""
"184","When Al-Mundhir bin Abu Usaid was born, he was brought to the Prophet (ﷺ) who placed him on his thigh. While Abu Usaid was sitting there, the Prophet (ﷺ) was busy with something in his hands so Abu Usaid told someone to take his son from the thigh of the Prophet (ﷺ) . When the Prophet (ﷺ) finished his job (with which he was busy), he said, Where is the boy?"""" Abu Usaid replied """"185"""",Abu Salamab. 'Abd al-Rahman reported:I along with the foster brother of 'A'isha went to her and he asked about the bath of the Apostle (ﷺ) because of sexual intercourse. She called for a vessel equal to a Sa' and she took a bath. and there was a curtain between us and her. She poured water on her head thrice and he (Abu Salama) said: The wives of the Apostle (ﷺ) collectedhair on their heads and these lopped up to ears (and did rot go beyond that)"""""
"185","[AI-translation] The hadith of ‘Āishah, when her brother asked her about the ghusl of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); she called for a vessel about the size of a sa‘, performed ghusl, and poured water over her head, while there was a curtain between us (as stated by Abū Salamah)."""
"186","Anas reported that Allah's Messenger (may peace he upon him) wed to make this supplication:\\"""" O Allah"""""""""""""
"187","Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said, As for me"""""
"188","While I and my fathwere with Jdb ij, dJ . Sofilof people were with him and they asked him about taking a bath- He replied, A SA' of watis sucient fyou."""" A mand said """"189"""",Jabir reported:The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) forbade to urinate in stagnant water"""""
"189","[AI-translation] The hadith of ‘Āishah, that a woman asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about her ghusl after menstruation, so he instructed her on how to perform ghusl. He said: ""Take a piece of musk and purify yourself with it."" She asked: ""How should I purify myself with it?"" He said: ""Purify yourself with it."" She asked: ""How?"" He said: ""Glory be to Allah! Purify yourself with it."" So I took it towards me and said: ""Should I rub it over the traces of the blood?"""""
"190","Fatima bint Abi Hubaish came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and said, O Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) I get persistent bleeding from the uterus and do not become clean. Shall I give up my prayers?"""" Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) replied """"191"""",It has been narrated on the authority of Ibn 'Umar who said:The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) forbade that one should travel to the land of the enemy taking the Qur'an with him"""""
"191","[AI-translation] The hadith of ‘Aishah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, that Umm Habibah experienced vaginal bleeding for seven years, so she asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about it, and he commanded her to perform ghusl, saying: ""This is a vein."" Consequently, she used to perform ghusl for every prayer."""
"192","Narrated Mu`adha:\n\nA woman asked `Aisha, \Should I offer the prayers that which I did not offer because of menses\"""" \n`Aisha said"""""
"193","(the daughter of Abu Talib) I visited Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) in the year of the Conquest of Mecca and found him taking a bath, and his daughter, Fatima was screening him. When I greeted him, he said, Who is it?"""" I replied"""""
"194","Abu Huraira reported from the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, who said: The Children of Israel used to bathe naked, and they would look at one another. Moses, however, would bathe alone. They said, """"By Allah, nothing prevents Moses from bathing with us except that he has scrotal hernia."""" So once, Moses went to bathe and placed his clothes on a rock. The rock ran away with his clothes. Moses chased after it saying, """"My clothes, O rock!"""" Until the Children of Israel saw Moses and they said, """"By Allah, there is nothing wrong with Moses."""" He took his clothes and began to strike the rock. Abu Huraira said, """"By Allah, he struck the rock six or seven times."""""""""""""
"195","Jabir b. 'Abdullah (Allah be pleased with both of them) reported that in the course of a journey Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) saw a man, people crowding around him and providing him a shade. Upon this he (the Holy Prophet) said:What is the matter with him? They said: He is a person observing fast. Whereupon the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: It is no righteousness that you fast on journey"""""
"196","Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) sent for a Ansari man who came with water dropping from his head. The Prophet (ﷺ) said, Perhaps we have forced you to hurry up"""""
"197","Narrated Ubai bin Ka`b:\n\nI asked Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) about a man who engages in sexual intercourse with his wife but does not \ndischarge. He replied, \He should wash the parts which comes in contact with the private parts of the \nwoman"""""
"198","`Abdullah bin `Umar said: """"A man got up in the mosque and said: O Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) 'At which place you order us that we should assume the Ihram?' Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) replied, 'The residents of Medina should assure the Ihram from Dhil-Hulaifa, the people of Syria from Al-Juhfa and the people of Najd from Qarn."""" Ibn `Umar further said, """"The people consider that Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) had also said, 'The residents of Yemen should assume Ihram from Yalamlam.' """" Ibn `Umar used to say, """"I do not: remember whether Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) had said the last statement or not?"""""""""""""
"199","The Prophet (ﷺ) said, Allah created Adam in His picture """"200"""",Narrated Ibn `Abbas:\n\nThe Prophet (ﷺ) was cupped on his head for an ailment he was suffering from while he was in a state of \nIhram. at a water place called Lahl Jamal. Ibn `Abbas further said: Allah s Apostle was cupped on his \nhead for unilateral headache while he was in a state of Ihram ."""""
"200","[AI-translation] The hadith of ‘Abdullah ibn ‘Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ate the shoulder of a sheep and then prayed without performing wudu."""
"201","I saw Allah's MessengqL.! d -, taking a piece of (cooked) mutton from the shouldregion and then h was called fSaldt (prayer). He put hi knife down and offered Salri witho repeating ablution """"202"""",Narrated Maimuna:\n\nThe Prophet (ﷺ) ate (a piece of) mutton from the shoulder region and then prayed without repeating the \nablution. """"203"""",Abu Huraira reported Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) as saying:I shall be pre-eminent amongst the descendants of Adam on the Day of Resurrection and I will be the first intercessor and the first whose intercession will be accepted (by Allah)"""""
"202","[AI-translation] The hadith of Maymunah, that the Prophet ﷺ ate a shoulder at her house, then prayed without performing wudu."""
"203","[AI-translation] The hadith of Ibn ‘Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ drank milk, then rinsed his mouth and said: ""Indeed, it has fat in it."""""
"204","My uncle asked Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) about a person who imagined to have passed wind during the prayer. Allah' Apostle replied: """"He should not leave his prayers unless he hears sound or smells something."""""""""""""
"205","The Prophet (ﷺ) saw a dead sheep which had been given in charity to a freed slave-girl of Maimuna, the wife of the Prophet (ﷺ) . The Prophet (ﷺ) said, Why don't you get the benefit of its hide?"""" They said"""""
"206","Abu Dharr reported:The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to me: O Abu Dharr, you would soon find after me rulers who would make their prayers dead. You should say prayer at its prescribed time. If you say prayer at its prescribed time that would be a supererogatory prayer for you, otherwise you saved your prayer"""""
"207","Ibn 'Abbas reported it on the authority of Maimuna, his mother's sister, that she said:I placed water near the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) to take a bath because of sexual intercourse. He washed the palms of his bands twice or thrice and then put his hand In the basin and poured water over his private parts and washed them with his left hand. He then struck his hand against the earth and rubbed it with force and then performed ablution for the prayer and then poured three handfuls of water on his head and then washed his whole body after which he moved aside from that place and washed his feet, and then I brought a towel (so that he may wipe his body). but he returned it"""""
"208","A man came to `Umar bin Al-Khattab and said, I became Junub but no water was available."""" `Ammar bin Yasir said to `Umar"""""
"209","A'isha (Allah be pleased with her) reported that a man said to Allah's Apostle (ﷺ):My mother died all of a sudden, and I think if she (could have the opportunity) to speak she would have (made a will) regarding Sadaqa'. Will I be entitled to reward if I give charity on her behalf? He (the Holy Prophet) said: Yes"""""
"210","Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) came across me and I was Junub. He took my hand and I went along with him till he sat down I slipped away, went home and took a bath. When I came back, he was still sitting there. He then said to me, """"O Abu Huraira! Where have you been?' I told him about it. The Prophet (ﷺ) said, """"Subhan Allah! O Abu Huraira! A believer never becomes impure."""""""""""""
"211","Whenever the Prophet (ﷺ) went to the lavatory, he used to say: """"Allahumma inni a`udhu bika min al-khubuthi wal khaba'ith."""""""" """"212"""",Narrated Anas:\n\nOnce the Iqama was pronounced and the Prophet (ﷺ) was talking to a man (in a low voice) in a corner of \nthe mosque and he did not lead the prayer till (some of) the people had slept (dozed in a sitting \nposture) ."""""
"212","[AI-translation] The hadith of Anas ibn Malik, who said: The prayer was established while the Prophet ﷺ was conversing privately with a man in a corner of the mosque, and he did not stand up for the prayer until the people had fallen asleep."""
